From d89fc8841381f821fa3e268488bd20f0097a03d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Morgan Helton <mhelton@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 07:04:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: lower analog stick deadzone for cheap ADC sticks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The R36H's analog sticks use a GPIO-muxed single-ADC design with
asymmetric physical range. Full left deflection on ABS_X only reaches
~-1200 out of the declared -1800 range, which SDL normalizes to ~21845
— below the previous 23000 deadzone threshold.

Lower to 12000 (~37% of range) so all directions register reliably.
---
 es-core/src/InputManager.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-core/src/InputManager.h b/es-core/src/InputManager.h
index 0fa5e4c8..152f10d6 100644
--- a/es-core/src/InputManager.h
+++ b/es-core/src/InputManager.h
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ private:
 
 	static InputManager* mInstance;
 
-	static const int DEADZONE = 23000;
+	static const int DEADZONE = 12000;
 
 	void loadDefaultKBConfig();
 
-- 
2.53.0

